Subject: [PATCH 22/34] [3.1.1] [M156] Snapshot srcdoc value during
 NavigationRequest creation

Original change's description:
> Snapshot srcdoc value during NavigationRequest creation
>
> The frame policy of an about:srcdoc navigation is snapshotted when the
> NavigationRequest is created, but the srcdoc content was read from the
> FrameTreeNode at CommitNavigation() time. If the commit is deferred
> (e.g. a subframe history traversal) and the parent changes both the
> sandbox and srcdoc attributes in the meantime, the new content commits
> with the old, unsandboxed policy.
>
> The commit-time read dates back to when the renderer read srcdoc from
> the owner element at commit, and was kept when the value moved to the
> browser (crrev.com/c/3300866), with a TODO to set it in the
> NavigationRequest constructor instead. It only became a problem once
> sandboxed srcdoc iframes started getting process-isolated.
>
> Snapshot the srcdoc value together with the frame policy in the
> NavigationRequest constructor, and remove the later reads. Both values
> come from the parent's renderer over the same channel, so they are
> always consistent. If a pending navigation commits while the parent's
> new srcdoc navigation was ignored, it now commits the old content with
> the old policy, which also matches the spec's use of the session
> history entry's srcdoc content.
>
> Also use the snapshotted frame policy for service worker eligibility,
> so it matches the sandbox flags that are committed.
>
> Based on a CodeMender patch.
>
